# Shared host Caddyfile — /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#
# This is the single entry file the native caddy.service loads (the mockingbuoy systemd drop-in points
# ExecStart at it). It holds ONLY global options + the conf.d import; every actual site lives in its own
# /etc/caddy/conf.d/*.caddy snippet (mockingbuoy.caddy, netbox.caddy, ...). setup.sh creates this file
# if it is absent and otherwise only ensures the `import` line exists — it never rewrites it, so your
# other sites are safe across a mockingbuoy redeploy.
#
# admin off: no admin API, so config changes are applied by `systemctl restart caddy` (a ~1 s blip on
# all sites), never a live API reload. This matches mockingbuoy's hardening; keep it unless you have a
# reason to enable graceful reload (see ops/lan/README.md).

{
	admin off
}

import /etc/caddy/conf.d/*.caddy
